-- The secretary or assistant secretary of the surviving corporation certifies on the agreement which sentence it was adopted
-- under, unless a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement.
-- src:1080 | If an agreement of merger is adopted by the constituent corporation surviving the merger, by action of its board of directors and without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to this subsection, the secretary or assistant secretary of that corporation shall certify on the agreement that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to this subsection and, (1) if it has been adopted pursuant to the first sentence of this subsection, that the conditions specified in that sentence have been satisfied, or (2) if it has been adopted pursuant to the second sentence of this subsection, that no shares of stock of such corporation were issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution approving the agreement of merger or consolidation, provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(f) (src:1080)
GIVEN `the agreement was adopted by the board of the surviving constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentence relied on`                                                                                              IS A `s 251(f) Sentence relied on`
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 251(f) What the secretary or assistant secretary certifies`
`s 251(f) what the secretary or assistant secretary must certify on the agreement` `the agreement was adopted by the board of the surviving constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(f)` `the sentence relied on` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the agreement was adopted by the board of the surviving constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(f)`)
       OR `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`
    THEN `nothing, because the agreement was not adopted under s 251(f) without a vote of the stockholders, or a certificate is filed in lieu of the agreement`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the sentence relied on`
         WHEN `the first sentence of s 251(f)`
              THEN `that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to s 251(f) and that the conditions specified in its first sentence have been satisfied`
         WHEN `the second sentence of s 251(f)`
              THEN `that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to s 251(f) and that no shares of stock were issued before the board adopted the resolution approving the agreement`

