§§ `s 251(g) a merger into a wholly-owned subsidiary to form a holding company`

-- "organizational documents" (src:1089): for a corporation its certificate of incorporation, for a limited liability company
-- its limited liability company agreement. The text defines it for those two; any other entity is not covered.
-- src:1089 | The term “organizational documents”, as used in paragraph (g)(7) of this section and in the preceding sentence, shall, when used in reference to a corporation, mean the certificate of incorporation of such corporation, and when used in reference to a limited liability company, mean the limited liability company agreement of such limited liability company.
