-- After a merger adopted without a vote under (g), three things hold for the stockholders (src:1090).
-- (i) "to the extent the restrictions of section 203 applied to the constituent corporation and its stockholders", they apply
-- to the holding company and its stockholders as though it were the constituent corporation. Where they did not apply, or the
-- merger was not adopted under (g), the clause says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1090 | From and after the effective time of a merger adopted by a constituent corporation by action of its board of directors and without any vote of stockholders pursuant to this subsection: (i) to the extent the restrictions of § 203 of this title applied to the constituent corporation and its stockholders at the effective time of the merger, such restrictions shall apply to the holding company and its stockholders immediately after the effective time of the merger as though it were the constituent corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the merger was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restrictions of s 203 applied to the constituent corporation and its stockholders at the effective time of the merger`    IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 203 (piece dg3)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(g)(i) the restrictions of s 203 apply to the holding company and its stockholders` `the merger was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)` `the restrictions of s 203 applied to the constituent corporation and its stockholders at the effective time of the merger` MEANS
    IF    `the merger was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)`
       AND `the restrictions of s 203 applied to the constituent corporation and its stockholders at the effective time of the merger`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (i) "all shares of stock of the holding company acquired in the merger shall for purposes of section 203 be deemed to have
-- been acquired at the time that the shares of stock of the constituent corporation converted in the merger were acquired."
-- src:1090 | all shares of stock of the holding company acquired in the merger shall for purposes of § 203 of this title be deemed to have been acquired at the time that the shares of stock of the constituent corporation converted in the merger were acquired …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the date on which the converted shares of the constituent corporation were acquired` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 251(g)(i) the date on which the holding company shares are deemed acquired for s 203` `the date on which the converted shares of the constituent corporation were acquired` MEANS
    `the date on which the converted shares of the constituent corporation were acquired`

-- (i) a stockholder who immediately before the effective time was not an interested stockholder within the meaning of
-- section 203 does not become one "solely by reason of the merger". For a stockholder who already was one, the proviso
-- says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1090 | provided further that any stockholder who immediately prior to the effective time of the merger was not an interested stockholder within the meaning of § 203 of this title shall not solely by reason of the merger become an interested stockholder of the holding company …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the stockholder was an interested stockholder within the meaning of s 203 immediately before the effective time of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 203 (piece dg3)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(g)(i) the merger alone makes the stockholder an interested stockholder of the holding company` `the stockholder was an interested stockholder within the meaning of s 203 immediately before the effective time of the merger` MEANS
    IF `the stockholder was an interested stockholder within the meaning of s 203 immediately before the effective time of the merger`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (ii) if the holding company has the corporate name of the constituent corporation, the old stock certificates represent the
-- shares of the holding company into which the constituent corporation's shares were converted. If the names differ the
-- clause says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:1090 | (ii) if the corporate name of the holding company immediately following the effective time of the merger is the same as the corporate name of the constituent corporation immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, the shares of capital stock of the holding company into which the shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation are converted in the merger shall be represented by the stock certificates that previously represented shares of capital stock of the constituent corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the corporate name of the holding company immediately after the effective time is the same as the corporate name of the constituent corporation immediately before it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(g)(ii) the stock certificates that represented the constituent corporation's shares represent the holding company's shares` `the corporate name of the holding company immediately after the effective time is the same as the corporate name of the constituent corporation immediately before it` MEANS
    IF `the corporate name of the holding company immediately after the effective time is the same as the corporate name of the constituent corporation immediately before it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- (iii) "to the extent a stockholder of the constituent corporation immediately prior to the merger had standing to institute
-- or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation, nothing in this section shall be deemed to
-- limit or extinguish such standing." A stockholder who had no standing is not covered (NOTHING): the clause does not give any.
-- src:1090 | (iii) to the extent a stockholder of the constituent corporation immediately prior to the merger had standing to institute or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation, nothing in this section shall be deemed to limit or extinguish such standing. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the stockholder had standing immediately before the merger to institute or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 251(g)(iii) the stockholder keeps standing to institute or maintain derivative litigation` `the stockholder had standing immediately before the merger to institute or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation` MEANS
    IF `the stockholder had standing immediately before the merger to institute or maintain derivative litigation on behalf of the constituent corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Certification, filing and representation (src:1090), as in (f).
-- src:1090 | If an agreement of merger is adopted by a constituent corporation by action of its board of directors and without any vote of stockholders pursuant to this subsection, the secretary or assistant secretary of the constituent corporation shall certify on the agreement that the agreement has been adopted pursuant to this subsection and that the conditions specified in the first sentence of this subsection have been satisfied, provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the agreement was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(g) the secretary or assistant secretary must certify that the agreement was adopted under s 251(g) and that its conditions are satisfied` `the agreement was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` MEANS
        `the agreement was adopted by the board of the constituent corporation without any vote of its stockholders pursuant to s 251(g)`
    AND (NOT `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`)

-- src:1090 | The agreement so adopted and certified shall then be filed and become effective, in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(g) and certified` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(g) the agreement so adopted and certified is then to be filed` `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(g) and certified` MEANS
    `the agreement has been adopted under s 251(g) and certified`

-- src:1090 | Such filing shall constitute a representation by the person who executes the agreement that the facts stated in the certificate remain true immediately prior to such filing.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 251(g) (src:1090)
GIVEN `the agreement adopted under s 251(g) and certified is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 251(g) the person who executes the agreement represents that the facts stated in the certificate remain true` `the agreement adopted under s 251(g) and certified is filed` MEANS
    `the agreement adopted under s 251(g) and certified is filed`
